# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Store Hub environment.  Copy to `.env` and fill in.  NEVER commit `.env`.
# All secrets are read ONLY through src/lib/env.ts (typed + Zod-validated).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- KicksDB (StockX source) -------------------------------------------------
# Sent verbatim as the `Authorization` header (no "Bearer " prefix).
# OPTIONAL: a shop selling only supplier-feed products (see GS_FEED_URL below)
# leaves it unset — KicksDB is then skipped everywhere instead of failing, and
# the feed is the sole source of truth.
# KICKS_SECRET=your-kicksdb-api-key
# Optional override; defaults to the public v3 base.
# KICKS_BASE_URL=https://api.kicks.dev/v3

# --- WooCommerce REST (store) ------------------------------------------------
# Powers the Sync tab: pull live store state and push price updates over the
# Woo REST API (wp-json/wc/v3). The key needs Read/Write on products.
# Optional: without them the Sync tab is disabled and the hidden file
# round-trip flow (/preview) remains the fallback.
# WOO_BASE_URL=https://shop.example.com
# WOO_CONSUMER_KEY=ck_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# WOO_CONSUMER_SECRET=cs_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# --- WordPress (wp/v2): the site's navigation menus --------------------------
# The Vetrina's Menu tab and /api/v1/menus talk to WordPress's own REST API,
# which the Woo keys cannot reach. An administrator's username (menus need
# edit_theme_options) and an Application Password of theirs: Users › Profile
# › Application Passwords, over HTTPS. WordPress 5.9+. Same site as
# WOO_BASE_URL. Optional: without them the Menu tab says what to set.
# See docs/menus.md.
# WP_APP_USER=admin
# WP_APP_PASSWORD=abcd efgh ijkl mnop qrst uvwx

# --- Vetrina (homepage editor) -----------------------------------------------
# The Vetrina edits the WordPress homepage through golden-hive-blocks >= 5.9.0
# (REST namespace wc-gh/v1), authenticated with the WOO_* keys above — the key
# needs Read/Write and its user needs manage_woocommerce. Set to "fixture" to
# try the editor against an in-memory demo shop instead (nothing is written).
# Default comes from src/config/hub.config.ts ("wordpress").
# VETRINA_SOURCE=fixture
# The Vetrina's own address: point it at this same app (DNS + reverse proxy)
# and set it here. On that host "/" is the Vetrina, and the operator tabs,
# API and cron endpoints are not served — they stay on the Hub's address.
# VETRINA_HOST=vetrina.resellpiacenza.shop

# --- GoldenSneakers feed -----------------------------------------------------
# The flat-assortment endpoint. Include your VAT/markup query params here:
# presented_price arrives FINAL and passes through the pricing engine unchanged.
# Products covered by the feed are OWNED by GoldenSneakers (sizes, prices,
# real stock). Optional: without these, upload the JSON manually on /feeds.
# GS_FEED_URL=https://www.goldensneakers.net/api/assortment-flat/?vat=22&markup=...
# GS_FEED_TOKEN=your-goldensneakers-bearer-token

# --- What the Hub does on its own -------------------------------------------
# The automatic sync is set in the Hub, not here: Feeds tab › Automatic sync ›
# Settings. How often the store follows the supplier feed (every 15 minutes
# out of the box), when the full daily sync runs, whether the KicksDB prices
# are written too, the safety limits, the orders pull, the automatic
# categories, self-repair and the healthchecks.io URLs. Saved there, a change
# applies within a minute, with nothing to restart.
#
# The variables that used to hold those settings (AUTO_SYNC, SCHEDULER_TIMES,
# SCHEDULER_FEEDS_MINUTES, AUTO_SYNC_MAX_CHANGES, …) are still read, but only
# as the starting values until the first save there; the Feeds tab lists the
# ones still set, so they can be removed.
#
# The one switch left here is the process's: run the scheduled syncs at all.
# Default: on in production, off in dev (npm run dev); set to override.
# SCHEDULER=on

# Shared secret for the cron endpoints (store pull / catalog refresh / GS
# sync) — only needed if you drive syncs from an EXTERNAL scheduler instead:
#   curl -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" https://host/api/cron/pull-store
# Unset = scheduled endpoints disabled (on-demand buttons still work).
# CRON_SECRET=change-me

# The programmatic API's callers (/api/v1/*: the Vetrina's actions as
# proposals, the log, undo — docs/api.md#tokens): one bearer token each, with
# what it may do — name:token:scopes, entries apart by commas, scopes from
# read+propose+confirm+undo+admin. Tokens of 24 characters or more
# (openssl rand -hex 32). Give confirm only to a token a person keeps: an
# assistant reads and proposes, the owner says yes. A wrong list stops the app.
# HUB_API_TOKENS=assistant:output-of-openssl-rand-hex-32:read+propose,phone:another-one:read+confirm+undo
# The single token from before: still a caller ("legacy"), with every scope —
# confirm included, so never an assistant's. Neither set = the API is disabled (503).
# HUB_API_TOKEN=output-of-openssl-rand-hex-32

# The one process that writes in the background — the scheduler, the
# Vetrina's actions, the automatic categories, the live sync (docs/deploy.md).
# Unset/writer on the app; web on any second process using the same database,
# which then serves but never starts those.
# HUB_ROLE=writer

# --- Sign-in -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The app has no login of its own. In production Authelia signs people in, in
# front of it, with an account per person (docs/auth.md), and Caddy adds this
# secret to every request it lets through. With it set, the app refuses any
# request without it. Unset = open app (local development).
# AUTH_PROXY_SECRET=output-of-openssl-rand-hex-32

# --- Persistence -------------------------------------------------------------
# Matches docker-compose.yml defaults for local development.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://kicks:kicks@localhost:5432/kicks
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# --- App ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default market and its currency mapping live in AppConfig; this is the
# bootstrap fallback used before a config row exists. Default IT.
# DEFAULT_MARKET=IT

# --- Diagnostics ----------------------------------------------------------
# The dev server prints the heap into its own console, beside the request log,
# whenever it moves by 25 MB or more — so the step that grows it can be read
# off the same output that shows the requests. Dev only. Set this to silence
# it; HEAP_WATCH_MS tunes the interval (default 5000).
# HEAP_WATCH=off
